      en: "Meragang Turtle Hatchery, established in 2005 along Brunei's coast, is dedicated to conserving sea turtles. It focuses on green and hawksbill turtles, collecting around 500 nests per season. The eggs are incubated in a protected area with controlled temperature and humidity, achieving an 85% hatching success rate. Hatchlings are released into the sea under moonlight to reduce predation. The hatchery also tags turtles to monitor migration patterns, with some tracked as far as the Philippines. Community engagement programs offer training for fishermen to handle accidentally caught turtles. Since inception, over 50,000 hatchlings have been released.",
